        <groundspeak:log id="684649392">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP365 Highlands&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A quick find along this quiet street.  What an impressive and fancy tree house across the street, complete with staircase!  There was a whole handful of dry grass in the divot, but that was easily removed and the information recorded.  Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683367648">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP365 Highlands&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our final cap find of the evening!  And a really quick one again, thanks to the context pic.  I knew where to inspect the ground and did so....finding a large hole with a bit of mud and leaves on top and a cap underneath.  :)  Another few quick pics and we were on our way.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I was told to put my phone down at this point.  lol  Done for the night!  TFTBC OFTH...first time I’ve found this many in one night.  I’m hoping to have a few more days like this this week before the ‘end’.  :)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681081322">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-25T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP365 Highlands

Grabbed a couple more BCPs today on the way to work this morning. Was nice and quiet with no one around. Pretty easy find. Only had to pull out a clump of leaves. The cap is pretty scarred up so had to interpret a couple of the numbers. 

Thanks outforthehunt for another BCP. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
